From these visible values we can compute the non-follower share: $\begin{aligned}
\frac{R_{\text{non-followers}}}{R_{\text{post}}}
&=
\frac{5{,}946}{23{,}424} \\
&\approx 0.254.\end{aligned}$ Thus, in the visible example, roughly one quarter of the reached accounts were not already followers. This percentage is a reconstruction from the screenshot, not a number spoken by the lecturer.

